-- SCOPE (binding): the depth-2 generator `Tools/ShippingSeqParentGenD2M.lean` (several DIFFERENT callees at the parent `P`, each callee `C_i`
-- with ONE leaf `G_i`, the `G_i` pairwise different).  CONCRETE examples only, not whole-class coverage.
--   * `topdiff2`: `wrap v w` and `wrap2 w v` (callees `wrap -> acc`, `wrap2 -> acc2`, genuinely different callees AND leaves);
--   * `topdiff3`: four calls (`wrap`, `wrap2`, `wrap`, `wrap2`) with different argument lists per callee, INTERLEAVED, several fields read;
--   * `topone`: a single-callee parent in a file that imports the new module (the one-callee elaborator still takes over);
--   * REFUSED, with the asserted reason: `topshare` (two callees call the SAME leaf `acc`), `topmix` (a leaf `cnt` next to the depth-2 callee `wrap`),
--     `topd3` (the next axis: a callee `wrap4` whose callee `wrap` has calls of its own: depth 3), `topdmem` (a memory in the parent).
-- Generated by `#machine_seq_parent_endpoint`; the call structure is ASSERTED by kernel-checked equations.  Not a general theorem; boundary
